---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { legal } from "../../data/legal";
const subject = encodeURIComponent(`Account deletion request for ${legal.appName}`);
const body = encodeURIComponent("I request deletion of my account and associated data.\nGoogle sign-in email: \nDisplay/account name (if any): \nDelete app-created Google Drive data (only if ownership and access can be verified): Yes / No\n");
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title={`Delete account and data | ${legal.appName}`} description={`How to request deletion of your ${legal.appName} account and data.`}>
<SiteHeader /><main id="main"><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Account</span><h1>Delete your account and data</h1><p><strong>{legal.appName}</strong> ({legal.packageName}) is operated by <strong>{legal.legalName}</strong> under the DoS Studio brand.</p></div></section>
<article class="prose">
<p>This page applies to CongTrinhSnap accounts. You can request deletion in the app or by email without reinstalling the app.</p>
<h2>1. Delete your account in the app</h2><ol><li>Open the app and sign in with the Google account you want to delete.</li><li>Open the <strong>Account</strong> tab, scroll down and select <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li><li>Review the data deletion options, including Google Drive data and local data.</li><li>Complete the confirmation and verification steps shown in the app.</li></ol>
<p>Your request is received after confirmation. Deletion at Google or other third-party systems may take additional time. Deleting local data affects only the device where you perform the action; other devices may need separate handling.</p>
<h2>2. Request deletion by email</h2><p>Email <a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`}><strong>{legal.supportEmail}</strong></a> from the Google address associated with your account. Use the subject “Account deletion request for {legal.appName}” and state the sign-in email and data you want deleted. If you no longer have access to that email, explain the situation so we can advise on reasonable verification. Never send your password, one-time code or full payment details.</p>
<h2>3. Processing time</h2><p>For a valid deletion request, we aim to respond within <strong>{legal.deletionInitialResponseWorkingDays} business days</strong> and complete deletion within <strong>{legal.deletionExecutionDays} days</strong>. Where coordination with processors or third parties is required, processing may take <strong>{legal.deletionThirdPartyDays} days</strong>. For a complex request, one extension of up to <strong>{legal.deletionExtensionDays} days</strong> may apply, with reasons communicated to you. These periods are subject to applicable Vietnamese law, including Decree 356/2025/ND-CP. Certain information may be retained where the law permits or requires it.</p>
<h2>4. Data deleted or handled</h2><ul><li>Firebase authentication account and associated profile data controlled by CongTrinhSnap.</li><li>Cloud project data you own, including project information, notes, annotations, members and encryption keys, subject to the app's deletion mechanism. Deleting an owner's project may remove access for other members.</li><li>Your membership in projects owned by others and invitations managed by the app.</li><li>Device information and Pro entitlement linked to your account, except minimum information retained lawfully for transaction verification or fraud prevention.</li><li>Files and folders created by the app in your Google Drive are deleted only when you select the relevant in-app option, the app still has access and the operation is supported. Otherwise, delete them directly in Google Drive. Removing a file you uploaded to a shared project may affect other members.</li><li>Local project data is deleted only from the device where you select that option. Data on other devices, exported ZIP/PDF files and content shared with other apps cannot be remotely deleted by us.</li></ul>
<h2>5. Data that may be retained</h2><ul><li>Hashed transaction identifiers and minimum related information may be retained as needed for transaction verification, fraud prevention or dispute resolution, then reviewed for deletion or de-linking unless retention is legally required.</li><li>Google Play retains payment records under Google's own policies and obligations.</li><li>Support emails may be retained as needed to resolve requests, complaints and legal obligations.</li><li>Data subject to mandatory legal retention or another lawful exception may be retained within the required scope and period.</li></ul><p>If some data cannot be deleted for a legitimate reason or because of a technical or provider-access limitation, we will explain the reason and available next steps where possible.</p>
<h2>6. Pro subscriptions</h2><p>Deleting your CongTrinhSnap account <strong>does not automatically cancel</strong> a Google Play subscription. To prevent renewal, manage or cancel it through the <a href={legal.playSubscriptionsUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play subscription page</a>. Cancellation and refunds are subject to Google Play rules.</p>
<h2>7. Delete only part of your data</h2><p>If supported by the app, you may delete individual photos, notes or projects, or leave a project without deleting your account. For other requests, email the support address above. See our <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.</p>
</article></main><SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
